\listmidiports prints the available MIDI output ports to
the traceback area, each with its number.
It takes no arguments:

\listmidiports

The output looks like this:

    MIDI out port 0: Midi Through:Midi Through Port-0 14:0
    MIDI out port 1: ...

The numbers printed are the ones used by \openmidiport,
\ctlchange, \pgmchange and the midiport method of an
instrument.
Call this command before opening a port, as the list of
ports is read only when this command is called. Call it
again if you connect a MIDI device later on.
